<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Solomon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Solomon was a king of ancient Israel, celebrated in the Bible for his wisdom and wealth. Ethiopian tradition holds that Menelik I was his son by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-of-sheba">Queen of Sheba</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomonic-dynasty">Solomonic dynasty</a> based its legitimacy on this claimed descent.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/solomon.jpg" alt="Solomon" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Simeon Solomon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Simeon_Solomon,_King_Solomon,_1872_or_1874,_NGA_76152_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
